WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.949 --> 00:00:05.410
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and recently
a new monster was spotted on the set of Series

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:06.410
8.

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:07.410
Don’t you just love it when they film outdoors.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:10.849
We don’t know who he is or what he’s all
about, but fans that were on the set that

00:00:10.849 --> 00:00:14.820
day started calling him “The Mole” just
because his claws look like they’re used

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:15.820
for digging.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:19.870
But it gives us a great excuse to talk about
the top 10 monsters we’d like to see come

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:20.870
back.

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:23.570
I love how when you see him walking around
like this it makes it look like he’s just

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:25.730
interrupting someone’s picnic in Cardiff.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:30.270
In related news, I’ve also got details on
some of the episodes and there’s a special

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:33.930
Doctor Who thing happening in April on the
Horror Channel.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:35.990
So I’m going to do two separate videos for
those.

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:37.590
And a new Q&amp;A video.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:40.700
Be sure to subscribe to get them if you’re
finding me for the first time.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.750
I’ll try to post them in the next week.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.920
So here’s the top 10 monsters I’d like
to see come back.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:47.500
Number 10 - The Beast.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:50.850
Easily one of the biggest if not scariest
monsters.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:55.690
He claimed to have existed since before the
normal universe existed.

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:58.810
And something about the way they’ve been
using the cracks makes me feel like ancient

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:03.260
old things, including the time lords, will
try to use them to coming back.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:07.450
Digital effects have evolved a lot since we
last saw him in series 2, but they did use

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:12.460
him again in a comic story where he escaped
to earth to try and get revenge on the 10th

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:13.460
Doctor.

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:18.020
One of the few thing really old monsters like
this are good for, aside from killing people,

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:19.209
is ancient knowledge.

00:01:19.209 --> 00:01:23.240
I’m really hoping the Doctor has a few good
Sherlock-style mysteries to solve.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:27.299
Clueing for looks all over time and space
just sounds like a lot of fun.

00:01:27.299 --> 00:01:29.659
Number 9 - The Ice Warriors

00:01:29.659 --> 00:01:33.899
The last time we saw Grand Marshall Skaldak
in Series 7 he was being rescued.

00:01:33.899 --> 00:01:37.359
We don’t know where they went, which means
they’re still at large.

00:01:37.359 --> 00:01:41.479
Even though the last time we saw him he was
having his Captain America de-thawed moment

00:01:41.479 --> 00:01:45.029
it’s possible that they Doctor could enlist
the aide of Skaldak to fight in a battle or

00:01:45.029 --> 00:01:46.029
two.

00:01:46.029 --> 00:01:47.909
Not all of Doctor Who’s monsters are villains.

00:01:47.909 --> 00:01:51.970
Despite evidence to the contrary.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:53.009
Number 8 - The Great Intelligence.

00:01:53.009 --> 00:01:54.070
Another ancient pre-universe character.

00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:58.139
We never really got a definitive answer as
to whether or not the Great Intelligence was

00:01:58.139 --> 00:02:01.719
really destroyed when it tried to enter the
Doctor’s timestream.

00:02:01.719 --> 00:02:05.299
Being so ancient and omniscient I find it
hard to believe that it would be destroyed

00:02:05.299 --> 00:02:06.429
so quickly.

00:02:06.429 --> 00:02:08.140
Number 7 - The Reapers.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:12.260
As much as the Doctor messes with the space
time continuum, I’m surprised they haven’t

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:13.380
come back sooner.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:18.129
The cracks are more of a tear in space than
a tear in time, so those wouldn’t necessarily

00:02:18.129 --> 00:02:24.370
bring them back, but it does seem like the
Doctor crosses his own time stream at least

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:28.760
once every series.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:38.590
Number 6 - The Pyroviles from The Fires of
Pompeii

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:43.019
How great would it be for The Doctor and Clara
to revisit Pompeii in some way, or at least

00:02:43.019 --> 00:02:48.060
visit somewhere that allows them to come back,
just as a nice nod to Capaldi’s other character

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.480
from that episode.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.939
Plus it would be a fun nod to Karen Gillan
too.

00:02:51.939 --> 00:02:55.709
I don’t expect her to cameo again until
the next anniversary special, but any reference

00:02:55.709 --> 00:02:59.890
to the original episode would be a subtle
reference to her character from before she

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:00.950
was cast as Amy Pond.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:05.320
There are a lot of rumors flying around that
Series 8 will pay some homage to Fires Of

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:07.180
Pompeii, but I haven’t seen any confirmation.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.900
There has been a nice fan made poster though.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:12.909
Number 5 - The Spiders including A New Great
One

00:03:12.909 --> 00:03:17.379
Originally seen in Planet of The Spiders,
this just sounds like it would be fun a la

00:03:17.379 --> 00:03:20.709
Martin Freeman had with the spiders of Mirkwood
during The Hobbit.

00:03:20.709 --> 00:03:23.560
Those spiders were much bigger than the ones
in planet of the spiders.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:25.659
But I just love the imagery they evoke.

00:03:25.659 --> 00:03:30.200
And the idea that at least in the original
story a giant spider queen is trying to ascend

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.069
to a higher state of existence.

00:03:32.069 --> 00:03:36.569
I think if they did make it back into a story
it would be something less cosmic.

00:03:36.569 --> 00:03:40.700
If series 8 is supposed to have a horror driven
tone, then I think spiders just building a

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:48.430
large lair feeding on people would be enough.

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:53.280
Number 4 - The Great Old Ones, who were from
classic who, but got a shout out during the

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:54.659
series 7 finale.

00:03:54.659 --> 00:03:59.269
They’re another pre-universe monster and
are really more effective as an idea, like

00:03:59.269 --> 00:04:02.690
the great intelligence, acting through different
physical bodies.

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:09.299
In classic who, their biology actually differed
quite a bit between members of the race, but

00:04:09.299 --> 00:04:14.150
they had the power to fundamentally change
the properties of the universe.

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:18.140
I think of them as being an inspiration for
the Q Continuum on Star Trek.

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:21.990
So when you think of them, imagine a more
sinister version of John DeLancie.

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:28.260
And instead of Patrick Stewart, imagine the
seventh doctor.

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:31.250
Number 3 - The Rest of The Pre-Universe Creatures.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:35.510
I already mentioned The Beast and The Old
Ones, but there are more things that existed

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:44.360
before the creation of our universe, the N-Universe.

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:48.360
Some of them like the ones I just mentioned
were able to travel into the new universe.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:50.980
Since the cracks exist all over time and space
now.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:55.540
I’m expecting other things besides the Time
Lords to use them to come in.

00:04:55.540 --> 00:05:00.380
That will always be a threat until the Doctor
either undoes the damage from when the cracks

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:01.570
were created.

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:06.250
Remember he rebooted the Universe.

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:08.350
So there’s no easy solution.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:13.530
Number 2 - The Time Lord Matrix.

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:17.940
Not really a monster, but much more relevant
as an idea given the current state of our

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:19.530
digital existence.

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:24.090
The last big story featuring the Matrix was
during The Ultimate Foe, which also featured

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.090
the Valeyard.

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:29.380
If you’re not familiar, the Time Lords use
the Matrix to store all their collected knowledge

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:31.060
and to predict the future.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:35.470
The Sixth Doctor was actually able to physically
enter it using the key of Rassilon.

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:39.430
Which is kind of funny and makes it seem like
the Wachowski’s totally ripped Doctor Who

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:40.430
off.

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:42.900
Since that movie was made 13 years after Ultimate
Foe.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:46.970
It’s not just a computer either, it’s
a micro universe.

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:49.760
Kind of like the pocket universe where Gallifrey
exists right now.

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:53.750
I don’t expect to see any more Time Lord
stories until the Doctor communicates with

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:57.040
them again or finds a safer way to restore
them to the normal universe.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.660
And I don’t think that’s going to happen
any time soon.

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:02.710
I do think he’ll speak to them again before
the end of Series 8.

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:06.680
and my number 1 monster I’d like to see
come back - The Valeyard.

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:08.080
The Dark Doctor.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:12.310
He escaped capture during Ultimate Foe and
while a lot of people think that The Master

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:13.980
is the Doctor’s ultimate foe.

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:16.060
I really think it’s the Valeyard.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:19.870
Since the Master is more of an anti-hero,
sometimes crazy person.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:23.860
As opposed to the Valeyard, who I see as more
of a black hat wearing villain.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:26.691
Who could be a greater enemy to you than your
own self.

00:06:26.691 --> 00:06:28.690
So now it’s your turn.

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:30.170
Which Monsters do you want to see Doctor Who
bring back.

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:32.960
As we saw from those behind the scenes pics.

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:38.570
Moffat is creating some new ones, so no matter
what I think series 8 will be a lot of fun.

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:40.980
At least if you enjoy horror stories.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:48.760
Like I said, I’m working on a Q&amp;A this weekend,
a breakdown of the series 8 episodes and there’s

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:49.873
a special horror channel marathon coming.

00:06:49.873 --> 00:06:52.580
So I’m going to do a video for my top 10
favorite scary classic doctor who stories.

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:53.580
Just classic who.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:57.440
Since series 8 is supposed to largely be inspired
by it.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:01.510
Right now click here to learn more about series
8 and click here for my next Doctor Who Q&amp;A.

00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:03.520
I’ll try to post that later this weekend.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:04.960
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:05.550
High fives!

